From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: ask mac80211 for unique station addresses on a radio

When a station turns up on a second BSS of a radio while the first BSS
still has it, hostapd tells the first BSS to drop it, but the old entry
leaves the kernel only when the status of the deauth frame is back, and
the new entry is added at once. ath11k_peer_create() takes the old peer
out of its hash, "expecting a disassoc soon", and sends the firmware a
peer create for an address it still holds a peer for on another vdev.
The IPQ5018 firmware (WLAN.HK.2.7.0.1) does not take that, on the
internal radio or on the QCN6122:

  ar_wal_peer.c:2899 Assertion is_graceful_to_handle failed
  remoteproc remoteproc0: crash detected in q6wcss: type fatal error

and the Q6 does not come back, so the radio is gone until a reboot - on
a board whose QCN6122 shares the Q6, both radios. A client that
deauthenticates before it changes the SSID never gets there; one that
just reappears on the other SSID does, the first time it tries.

Set IEEE80211_HW_NEEDS_UNIQUE_STA_ADDR, so that mac80211 does not let a
second entry for an address exist on the radio; with the mac80211 patch
that goes with this one it takes the old entry out, peer and all, before
the new one goes in. The hardware is registered per radio, so a station
moving to the other band is not affected.

Reported-by: kflush (OpenWrt forum)
Link: https://forum.openwrt.org/t/ipq5018-nss-offload-on-kernel-6-18-with-the-upstream-ethernet-stack-gl-b3000/253014/660
Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -11144,6 +11144,7 @@ static int __ath11k_mac_register(struct ath11k *ar)
 	ieee80211_hw_set(ar->hw, SUPPORTS_TX_FRAG);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(ar->hw, REPORTS_LOW_ACK);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(ar->hw, HAS_TX_QUEUE);
+	ieee80211_hw_set(ar->hw, NEEDS_UNIQUE_STA_ADDR);
 
 	if (ath11k_frame_mode == ATH11K_HW_TXRX_ETHERNET) {
 		ieee80211_hw_set(ar->hw, SUPPORTS_TX_ENCAP_OFFLOAD);
